# Review 3 #13 (M2c): a camera flight is steps of the one 60 Hz driver.
# Before, `fly` moved the camera and wrote frames without stepping the
# session: sand hung in the air and the simulation tick stood still for
# the whole flight, and frames written while blocks fell drew a stale list
# of them. Here a sand block is knocked off its support and a one-second
# recorded flight follows: the block must land during the flight, the tick
# must advance by 20, the sky clock by skyspeed x 1 s, and the written
# frames must draw the falling block. Needs ffmpeg (as the showcase does).
#
# Site: the flat m2a-sand patch, row J = 57531: S = 107155 and T = 107156
# have level ground.

mode walk
atblock 2 107156 57531 2000
assert on_ground == true
assert block_rel[0,0,-1] != air
# Two sand blocks on T's ground: one at the feet, one above it.
mode fly
select 4
assert selected_block == sand
aim 0 0 -0.5
tap place
assert block_rel[0,0,0] == sand
hold space 0.05
aim 0 0 -0.5
tap place
assert block_rel[0,0,0] == sand
assert block_rel[0,0,-1] == sand
# From S, knock out the bottom one: the top one falls a layer.
mode walk
atblock 2 107155 57531 2000
assert on_ground == true
lookaxis +i 0
aim 1 0 0.2
assert crosshair == sand
tap break
assert block_rel[1,0,0] == air
assert block_rel[1,0,1] == sand
assert falling == 0
state before_fly
assert sim_tick == 1
# The sky held so far (skyspeed 0): the clock at 12:00 at the spawn.
assert sky_seconds ~ 1142.5417 0.001
# A one-second flight, recorded, with the sky at 60x.
target rel 1 0 1
keyrel 1 30 -j 15
skyspeed 60
record m2c-fly.mp4 30
fly none target
stop
assert sim_tick == 21
assert falling == 0
assert landings == 1
assert video_falling_drawn_max >= 1
assert sky_speed == 60
# 60 steps at 60x: one game minute.
assert sky_seconds ~ 1202.5417 0.001
state after_fly
skyspeed 0
# The block landed on T's ground (absolute: the camera is elsewhere now).
mode walk
atblock 2 107155 57531 2000
assert block_rel[1,0,0] == sand
assert block_rel[1,0,1] == air
